# Museum multispectral scan ingestion

This workspace selects payload files, starts transfers, records queue and
progress history, and paints progress for its open panel. Runtime: CPython 3.8.10.
Dependencies: Python standard library. See src for the session/component entry API.

Selecting a file creates a visit. Retry replaces the physical attempt without
opening another visit. Selecting the same file object again opens a new visit.
The source is shared by attempts and visits for that file. start may emit cached
packets synchronously; decoding yields a full frame, immediately or later.
Decode completion order can differ from packet arrival order.

recordProgress appends transfer history; showProgress paints the open panel.
Queue records, notices, cancellation, retry, navigation, and cleanup retain
their existing behavior. Queue records are {fileId, attemptId, visitId, kind}
unless a separate authorization adds byteCount from file.size.

One startup window is relevant to this maintenance request: start may emit
more than one packet synchronously. A showProgress callback may select or hide
another visit before start returns, while its caller has not yet received the
returned cleanup handle.

The same source service also has a diagnostic consumer, Telemetry/
collectProgressTelemetry, whose existing live delta observations are separate
from the panel. Keep its existing behavior during this maintenance.
Removing a listener commits removal before calling the host detach callback;
that callback may synchronously select, hide or dispose. Repeated removal is
inert. Host callbacks execute synchronously unless explicitly deferred.

Files have stable object identity and immutable id/size during these commands.
A full frame replaces displayed state; loaded values can decrease or reset.
A decode result resolves once; rejected decode and physical transfer completion
are outside this embedding's model. Each workspace has its own lifetime.

Environment.call/bind provides a synchronous source embedding: listen(file
 token, callback token) returns a subscription, start can invoke it before
returning, and unlisten may reenter navigation. decode(file token, packet,
completion token) returns {deferred:false,frame} or {deferred:true}. Deferred
completion invokes the bound native closure on an explicit later host turn.
Transport receives a physical cancellation observer corresponding to the
native attempt state; cancel is idempotent. The wire embedding interns file
objects and forwards source/sink calls. Go uses context cancellation; the other
native ports use object flags. No native DOM/Promise runtime is claimed.
class Subscription:
    @staticmethod
    def attach(env,file,active,audit,view):
        if not file['feed']:return lambda:None
        def listener(packet):
            order=active()
            def deliver(frame):
                audit(frame);view(frame,order)
            value=env.call('decode',file['token'],packet,env.bind(deliver))
            if not value['deferred']:deliver(value['frame'])
        callback=env.bind(listener)
        env.call('start',file['token'])
        subscription=env.call('listen',file['token'],callback)
        return lambda:env.call('unlisten',file['token'],subscription)
# A session owns visits, while attempt closures own source and decode callbacks.
class Visit:
    def __init__(self, number, file):self.id=number;self.file=file;self.handle=None
class Attempt:
    def __init__(self, env, file, number, active=lambda:1, audit=lambda f:None, view=lambda f,o:None):
        self.env=env;self.file=file;self.number=number;self.aborted=False;self.stop=lambda:None
        env.call('transport',file['token'],number)
        self.stop=Subscription.attach(env,file,active,audit,view)
        if self.aborted:self.stop()
    def cancel(self):
        if self.aborted:return
        self.aborted=True;self.stop();self.env.call('cancel',self.file['token'],self.number)
class Session:
    def __init__(self,env):self.env=env;self.visit=None;self.serial=0;self.attempts=0;self.tasks=[];self.disposed=False
    def current(self,v):return self.visit is v
    def enqueue(self,v,kind):
        self.attempts+=1;n=self.attempts
        entry=dict(fileId=v.file['id'],attemptId=n,visitId=v.id,kind=kind)
        self.env.call('record',entry)
        def audit(frame):self.env.call('recordProgress',dict(fileId=v.file['id'],attemptId=n,frame=frame))
        def view(frame,order):
            if self.current(v):self.env.call('showProgress',dict(fileId=v.file['id'],attemptId=n,frame=frame))
        h=Attempt(self.env,v.file,n,lambda:0,audit,view);self.tasks.append(h);return h
    def notice(self,v,h):
        self.env.call('showQueued',dict(fileId=v.file['id'],attemptId=h.number,visitId=v.id,status='queued'))
    def release(self,v):
        h=v.handle;v.handle=None
        if h:h.cancel()
    def select(self,file):
        if self.disposed:return None
        self.serial+=1;request=self.serial;old=self.visit;self.visit=None
        if old:self.release(old)
        if self.disposed or self.serial!=request:return None
        v=Visit(request,file);self.visit=v;h=self.enqueue(v,'select')
        if self.current(v):v.handle=h;self.notice(v,h)
        else:h.cancel()
        return h
    def retry(self):
        v=self.visit
        if not v or not v.handle or self.disposed:return None
        v.handle.cancel()
        accepted=v
        h=self.enqueue(accepted,'retry')
        if self.current(accepted):accepted.handle=h
        else:h.cancel()
        if self.current(accepted):self.notice(accepted,h)
        return h
    def hide(self):
        self.serial+=1;old=self.visit;self.visit=None
        if old:self.release(old)
    def dispose(self):
        if self.disposed:return
        self.disposed=True;self.hide()
        for h in self.tasks:h.cancel()
    def snapshot(self):
        v=self.visit
        return dict(visitId=v.id if v else None,fileId=v.file['id'] if v else None,attemptId=v.handle.number if v and v.handle else None,disposed=self.disposed,attempts=self.attempts)

